    {
      "id": "01",
      "title": "One signature, many jobs",
      "question": "What does FastAPI do with the type hints on an endpoint?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "FastAPI, question one. What does FastAPI actually do with the type hints on an endpoint function, from request to response? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "What does FastAPI do with your <em>type hints</em>?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Uvicorn, an ASGI server, receives the request, and Starlette routes it to your function. Then FastAPI reads the signature: shop ID appears in the path, so it's a path parameter, and item is a Pydantic model, so it comes from the JSON body. Pydantic validates and converts everything. If anything is wrong, the client gets an automatic four twenty-two, listing each error, and your function never runs. Next, dependencies are resolved, once per request. Then your function runs, and its return value is filtered through the response model, so fields like a password hash never leak. The same type hints also generate the OpenAPI schema, and interactive docs.",
