        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "In code: shop ID is in the path, so it's a path parameter. Item is a model, so it's the body. A simple type that isn't in the path, like verbose, becomes a query parameter. The database comes from a dependency. And the response model filters the result.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Where each parameter <em>comes from</em>",
            "file": "items.py",
            "tag": "FastAPI",
            "lang": "python",
            "size": 21,
            "width": 1180,
            "code": "@app.post(\"/items/{shop_id}\", response_model=ItemOut, status_code=201)\nasync def create_item(\n    shop_id: int,                                   # in the path → path param\n    item: ItemIn,                                   # a model → JSON body\n    verbose: bool = False,                          # anything else → query\n    db: Annotated[DB, Depends(get_db)],             # injected dependency\n):\n    if item.price <= 0:\n        raise HTTPException(400, \"price must be positive\")\n    return await db.insert(shop_id, item)           # filtered by ItemOut",
